      "name": "a message refused for its leash has still spent its number",
      "law": "The seq and the leash",
      "obligations": ["VIII-3", "VIII-9", "XII-1", "VII-4", "XII-14"],
      "derivation": "The same voice, correctly addressed, carrying seq 1 and an allowance whose time budget is zero. Article XII spends the seq at step 5 and the leash at step 6, in that order. Article VIII: \"a time budget at or below zero ... is silence\", and \"Honoured means the number is consumed, and nothing later gives it back — a message refused at routing or for its leash has still spent it.\" So: silence on the wire, and a mark that has moved to 1. The way back is learned here too, because Article XII refreshes it \"between the seq and the leash\" — \"a message refused for its leash still arrived and still spent its number.\" This is the exchange that makes step order visible, because the silence here is byte-for-byte the silence above and the state is not.",
